Release packaging for the trading node (docs/NODE_RUNBOOK.md). Apply on main after
feature/live-trading is merged, from the repository root:

    git apply --check ops/node_release.patch && git apply ops/node_release.patch

then delete this file in the same commit. It changes two shared files, which the node's
deployment work does not edit directly while the integration is in progress.

ops/build_release.sh
  0. The version check. packages/midfreq-engine (0.1.0, merged from feature/native-engine via
     integration/pre-oms) disagrees with the shipped packages (0.1.1), so the build stops at
     its first step: "packages disagree on the version ... run ops/set_version.sh". The engine
     is not shipped (the wheel loop skips it), so the check now skips it too; set_version.sh
     still sets every package's version, the engine's included.
  1. The wheel count. The script ends with `[ "$n" -eq 6 ]`. Once midfreq-trading is merged,
     packages/ holds eight packages; the loop skips midfreq-engine and builds seven wheels, so
     every release build (and CI's `vm` job, which builds the bundle on every push) fails with
     "expected 6 wheels, built 7". It now expects one wheel per package under packages/ except
     midfreq-engine, at the release's version, and names any that is missing.
  2. The node's launcher. ops/run_node.sh is not copied into the bundle, so a release cannot run
     the node from the schedule (nor node_startup_check.sh's launcher dry run). Added to ops/.
  3. The startup checks. ops/README.md says startup_check.sh ships in releases from 0.1.2, but
     the copy line never included it; node_startup_check.sh is new. Both added to ops/vm/.
  Already right, no change: defaults/config/ is `git archive HEAD config`, so the committed
  config/node_sp100.yaml, config/node_hk_paper.yaml, config/corporate_actions.json and the new
  holiday fields of config/venues.json all ship; the midfreq-trading wheel carries the
  `midfreq-node` console script (its [project.scripts]), which pip installs into .venv/bin.

ops/vm/install_release.sh (smoke test)
  The smoke test imported the six original packages only, so a release whose node could not
  even import would still be made current. It now also imports midfreq.trading.node and
  midfreq.trading.cli, and runs `midfreq-node check-config` on every config/node_*.yaml the
  release ships (with the release's own defaults as MIDFREQ_ROOT, as the import line does):
  the console script exists, the configurations are valid for this release's code (unknown
  risk/OMS settings are refused) and every component imports, without connecting to anything.
  On failure it prints check-config's output. CI's `vm` job runs this on Python 3.10 with
  requirements-vm.txt, i.e. the node's code is checked on the VM's interpreter and pins.

ops/vm/requirements-vm.txt: no change. midfreq-trading imports pandas and PyYAML (both pinned);
its components reach the venue only through midfreq.data's connectors, whose Moomoo side uses
the moomoo SDK (moomoo_api==10.8.6808, pinned; the research environment has 10.2.6208) and
whose ccxt side imports ccxt lazily, only when an OKX/ccxt account is configured (none on the VM).
numpy, pyarrow, tzdata, pydantic and python-dotenv, which the packages below it use, are pinned.

